        "evidence": [
          "`call_codex.py` and `codex_lm.py` both orchestrate `codex exec` subprocess calls with separate command assembly and error mapping.",
          "`find_plan.py` and `gather_implementation.py` each implement their own subprocess invocation patterns for git with local timeout/error semantics.",
          "No shared execution/policy layer exists for subprocess-backed tooling, so behavior diverges by script and creates broad ripple when external CLI contracts change."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Extract a shared infrastructure module (for example, `scripts/lib/cli_exec.py`) that standardizes subprocess execution, timeout defaults, and structured error mapping, then have all four scripts consume that boundary rather than owning ad-hoc subprocess policy.",
