      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Async API is implemented as sync pass-through, adding interface ceremony without async behavior.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "ai_generated_debt",
        "related_files": [
          "fando-plan/scripts/codex_lm.py",
          "fando-plan/scripts/run_parallel_reviews.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "CodexLM.aforward() is declared async but directly returns self.forward(...), which still runs blocking subprocess.run().",
          "The surrounding review pipeline already parallelizes at thread level, so this async surface is redundant and potentially misleading."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either remove aforward() and keep a clearly sync LM adapter, or implement true async execution (async subprocess or executor) so interface and runtime behavior match.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Removed the misleading aforward() async wrapper from CodexLM. The method was declared async but just delegated to the synchronous forward(), which runs blocking subprocess.run(). Since the surrounding pipeline uses ThreadPoolExecutor for parallelism, the async interface was redundant and potentially misleading. CodexLM now has a clear synchronous interface matching its subprocess-based runtime behavior.",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-28T07:10:08+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-28T07:10:08+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-02-28T10:41:44+00:00",
