          "`run_parallel_reviews_dspy()` immediately feeds that text into `parse_findings()` to recover structured counts/items."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Return a typed findings object directly from DSPy path (or a shared dataclass schema) and use text formatting only for terminal rendering.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Created prediction_to_parse_result() function that converts DSPy predictions directly to ParseResult (structured format), bypassing the markdown roundtrip. Updated run_parallel_reviews_dspy() to use direct structured conversion instead of prediction \u2192 markdown \u2192 parse_findings(). This eliminates inefficient text serialization and parsing while maintaining all functionality.",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-28T10:35:13+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-28T10:35:13+00:00",
