    "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::parallel_review_backend_duplication::a2579c27": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::parallel_review_backend_duplication::a2579c27",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Parallel review pipeline is duplicated per backend, creating drift-prone control flow.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "design_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "fando-plan/scripts/run_parallel_reviews.py",
          "fando-plan/scripts/dspy_reviewers.py",
          "fando-plan/scripts/call_codex.py",
          "fando-plan/scripts/parse_findings.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "run_parallel_reviews.py has separate backend paths that each perform execution, error mapping, parse_findings invocation, and severity aggregation (101-173 and 247-306).",
          "The DSPy path relies on string pattern checks (`\"Error:\"` and exact section text) to detect failure states (286-289), while codex path uses structured `CodexResult.error`, showing divergent contracts.",
          "Both paths then feed near-identical summary and output assembly logic (460-490), increasing update cost when output schema changes."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce a backend adapter contract returning a normalized `ReviewResult` (success/error/findings/output), then run one shared aggregation/output path independent of backend type.",
        "reasoning": ""
